This repository neither contains nor distributes third-party binaries.
Each user downloads the components they choose from the official distribution
sites with scripts/fetch-bundle.sh, builds their own offline bundle, and brings
it into their network themselves. The components remain under their own licenses:

- Open source: Node.js, pi coding agent, fd, ripgrep, jq, just, hurl, glab, gh,
  agent-browser, obscura, Chromium, usql, dbhub.
- Fonts: D2Coding (NAVER Corp., SIL Open Font License 1.1). The bundle carries the
  font files and their license as vendor/fonts/d2coding/OFL.txt.
- Not open source (license terms are shown and must be accepted at fetch time;
  a bundle containing them is for the user's own use): Oracle SQLcl (Oracle Free
  Use Terms and Conditions), Chrome for Testing (Google Chrome Terms of Service).
